WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:15.232
"Wow," Henry said.

2
00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:18.052
"Who would leave a message like that?"

3
00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:20.693
"I don't know," Maggie said.

4
00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:23.594
"I thought everyone in town loved the summer parade."

5
00:00:24.474 --> 00:00:25.234
Cole shrugged.

6
00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:27.375
"Maybe someone is joking around."

7
00:00:27.395 --> 00:00:30.556
"If it's a joke, it's not very funny."

8
00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:32.569
Henry stared at the message.

9
00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:37.271
"It sounds more like a threat."

10
00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:38.072
Cole grinned.

11
00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:40.633
"Are you trying to turn it into a mystery, Henry?"

12
00:00:41.514 --> 00:00:46.176
Just then two teenage girls, Jill and Ashley, raced up to the lemonade stand.

13
00:00:46.196 --> 00:00:48.618
"Oh my gosh!

14
00:00:48.638 --> 00:00:49.878
Did you guys hear what happened?"

15
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:50.839
Jill asked.

16
00:00:51.759 --> 00:00:54.741
Ashley continued before The Lemonade Detectives could respond.

17
00:00:54.761 --> 00:00:57.623
"Someone broke into the shed where Mrs.

18
00:00:57.703 --> 00:00:59.123
Sweet is keeping her float!"

19
00:00:59.404 --> 00:00:59.944
she cried.

20
00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:02.064
"Huh?" Cole said.

21
00:01:02.084 --> 00:01:04.185
"Why would someone do that?"

22
00:01:04.205 --> 00:01:06.666
"Was the float damaged?"

23
00:01:07.026 --> 00:01:07.826
Henry asked.

24
00:01:08.706 --> 00:01:09.626
Jill shook her head.

25
00:01:09.646 --> 00:01:11.107
"We're not sure.

26
00:01:11.127 --> 00:01:17.148
Mrs. Sweet is keeping her float top secret until the parade, so she didn't tell us exactly what

27
00:01:17.188 --> 00:01:20.789
happened. But she's afraid that someone wants to sabotage it."

28
00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.570
Just then Ashley's cell phone rang.

29
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.371
"Oops, we have to go," she said.

30
00:01:26.391 --> 00:01:27.711
"Come on, Jill."

31
00:01:28.712 --> 00:01:29.792
The girls raced off.

32
00:01:30.588 --> 00:01:31.588
Maggie looked worried.

33
00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:33.289
"This is bad.

34
00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.771
What if someone is trying to sabotage all the floats?"

35
00:01:38.071 --> 00:01:39.732
"Why would anyone do that?"

36
00:01:40.052 --> 00:01:41.332
Cole sounded skeptical.

37
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:43.013
Maggie shrugged.

38
00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.434
"Maybe to win those great prizes.

39
00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:49.856
We should probably investigate before someone tries to destroy our float!"

40
00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.697
"How could anybody do that?"

41
00:01:52.937 --> 00:01:53.557
Cole said.

42
00:01:53.577 --> 00:01:55.818
"It's inside your house, Maggie.

43
00:01:56.618 --> 00:02:00.200
Besides, we don't have time to mess around with a mystery right now."

44
00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:01.452
He laughed.

45
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:04.813
"I don't think this is a mystery anyway.

46
00:02:04.993 --> 00:02:05.573
Right, Henry?"

47
00:02:06.474 --> 00:02:08.114
Henry didn't answer for a second.

48
00:02:09.074 --> 00:02:12.235
He was thinking about that threatening message on the town website.

49
00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:16.176
"Maybe we should go talk to my dad," he said.

50
00:02:16.196 --> 00:02:19.597
"Just in case something really is going on."

51
00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:22.178
"Good idea," Maggie said.

52
00:02:22.198 --> 00:02:24.759
"Uncle Kevin is a newspaper reporter.

53
00:02:25.619 --> 00:02:28.500
It's his job to know about weird stuff happening around town."

54
00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.901
"Fine." Cole shrugged.

55
00:02:30.921 --> 00:02:32.762
"You two go talk to him.

56
00:02:33.183 --> 00:02:35.064
I'll stay here and watch the lemonade stand."

57
00:02:38.526 --> 00:02:42.829
Henry and Maggie walked toward the main part of town, where the newspaper office was located.

58
00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.491
On the way they passed Eddie's house.

59
00:02:46.492 --> 00:02:49.974
The garage door was shut; no music was coming from behind it.

60
00:02:49.994 --> 00:02:54.537
"I guess Snake's band isn't practicing today," Henry said.

61
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:57.880
He told Maggie about seeing the band the day before.

62
00:02:59.024 --> 00:03:00.405
Maggie stared at the garage.

63
00:03:00.425 --> 00:03:05.389
"I wonder if Snake and his band members should be suspects," she said.

64
00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:08.891
"He seemed really excited about winning the contest."

65
00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:12.214
"Lots of people want to win," Henry said.

66
00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:16.537
"That doesn't mean all of them want to sabotage the other floats."

67
00:03:16.557 --> 00:03:18.638
"Maybe not."

68
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:19.659
Maggie shrugged.

69
00:03:19.679 --> 00:03:22.321
"But Snake seemed kind of sneaky."

70
00:03:23.222 --> 00:03:24.262
Henry didn't answer.

71
00:03:24.963 --> 00:03:26.344
He thought Snake seemed okay.

72
00:03:27.264 --> 00:03:30.826
But when Maggie got an idea in her head, it could be hard to change her mind.

73
00:03:33.928 --> 00:03:36.829
A few minutes later, they reached the newspaper office.

74
00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.091
"Hi, Henry," the receptionist said.

75
00:03:40.111 --> 00:03:42.172
"Your dad just left."

76
00:03:42.192 --> 00:03:45.314
"Really?" Henry was disappointed.

77
00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.355
"Do you know when he'll be back?

78
00:03:48.476 --> 00:03:51.637
We wanted to ask him some questions about the summer parade."

79
00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:56.020
The receptionist pointed to a young man who had just come into the lobby.

80
00:03:57.212 --> 00:04:00.734
"If it's about the parade, maybe Jackson can help," she said.

81
00:04:00.754 --> 00:04:03.536
"He's assigned to cover that story."

82
00:04:04.456 --> 00:04:06.377
Henry had met Jackson several times.

83
00:04:07.438 --> 00:04:10.019
He walked over to the reporter with Maggie right behind him.

84
00:04:12.081 --> 00:04:13.962
Jackson smiled when he saw them coming.

85
00:04:13.982 --> 00:04:16.263
"Hi, Henry," he said.

86
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:17.424
"Hi, Maggie.

87
00:04:18.104 --> 00:04:18.504
What's up?

88
00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:22.326
Did The Lemonade Detectives uncover an exciting crime for me to write about?"

89
00:04:22.346 --> 00:04:24.768
"Maybe," Henry said.

90
00:04:25.532 --> 00:04:27.933
"Is it true that you're covering the parade this year?"

91
00:04:27.953 --> 00:04:29.353
"That's right."

92
00:04:29.633 --> 00:04:31.434
Jackson didn't sound very excited.

93
00:04:32.494 --> 00:04:33.634
Henry wasn't surprised.

94
00:04:34.314 --> 00:04:38.256
His father said Jackson was always looking for important and dramatic stories.

95
00:04:39.276 --> 00:04:42.577
Unfortunately for him, there weren't very many of those in Belltown.

96
00:04:42.597 --> 00:04:45.397
"We heard someone might have tampered with Mrs.

97
00:04:45.437 --> 00:04:47.338
Sweet's float," Maggie spoke up.

98
00:04:48.498 --> 00:04:49.419
Jackson nodded.

99
00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:50.499
"I heard it too.

100
00:04:51.379 --> 00:04:54.480
Actually, I was just on my way over to the Sweet Shop to talk to her.

101
00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.761
You two can come along, if you like."

102
00:04:57.781 --> 00:04:59.222
The three of them headed outside.

103
00:05:02.984 --> 00:05:05.646
you think someone is trying to sabotage Mrs.

104
00:05:05.726 --> 00:05:06.526
Sweet's float?"

105
00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.408
Henry asked as they walked toward the Sweet Shop.

106
00:05:10.408 --> 00:05:11.509
Jackson shook his head.

107
00:05:11.529 --> 00:05:12.309
"I doubt it.

108
00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.831
Her float was probably damaged by animals or something.

109
00:05:16.851 --> 00:05:19.693
Or maybe she just got confused and forgot to lock the shed."

110
00:05:20.694 --> 00:05:21.814
Henry thought about that.

111
00:05:22.474 --> 00:05:25.096
Mrs. Sweet was always joking about her bad memory.

112
00:05:26.056 --> 00:05:29.001
She often said she'd forget her head if it wasn't attached to her neck!

113
00:05:30.122 --> 00:05:30.583
Could Mrs.

114
00:05:30.623 --> 00:05:33.447
Sweet's forgetfulness explain what Jill and Ashley had said?

115
00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:37.213
Henry was still wondering about it when they reached the Sweet Shop.

116
00:05:38.214 --> 00:05:41.980
Just then there was a blood-curdling scream from the alley beside the shop!
